  "discussion": {
    "headline": "breezy and cool start to autumn",
    "dateLine": "2:00 p.m. Tuesday, September 22, 2026",
    "excerpt": "In the wake of Sunday night's cold frontal passage, northeasterly winds ushered much cooler and drier air into the Lower Susquehanna Valley on Monday. Under mostly cloudy skies, temperatures only peaked in the mid 60s to low 70s from west-to-east across the region. A few showers dampened northern MD and south-central PA Monday afternoon and evening, but steadier rain held off until the overnight hours. …",
